Portions adapted from Orange Data Mining

Some parts of this add-on are adapted from the source code of Orange Data
Mining, Copyright (C) Bioinformatics Laboratory, Faculty of Computer and
Information Science, University of Ljubljana, licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later. Those portions keep Orange's copyright and
license; the additional terms above do not apply to them. Each affected file
says so in its header:

- orangecontrib/orange_gualbe_toolbox/widgets/owtestscorepro.py, adapted from
  Orange/widgets/evaluate/owtestandscore.py: the handling of the multiple
  Learner input (set, insert and remove learners keyed by input order), the
  lists of resampling options (numbers of folds, repetitions and training
  sizes), the names of the inputs, outputs and resampling settings, and the
  structure of the resampling choices and their messages.
- orangecontrib/orange_gualbe_toolbox/widgets/_tsp_engine.py, adapted from
  Orange/widgets/evaluate/owtestandscore.py: the construction of the Orange
  samplers for each resampling method and the check that training and test
  data share the target variable.
- orangecontrib/orange_gualbe_toolbox/widgets/_tsp_window.py, adapted from
  Orange/evaluation/testing.py: WindowValidation.__call__ follows the
  structure of Validation.__call__ (preparation of the folds, training and
  testing loop and construction of the Results object).
- orangecontrib/orange_gualbe_toolbox/widgets/owfileimport.py, adapted from
  Orange/widgets/data/owfile.py: the list of recent files with Orange's
  sample datasets, the search paths, the use of RecentPathsWComboMixin, the
  update of relative paths when the workflow is saved and the handling of
  dropped files and URLs.
- orangecontrib/orange_gualbe_toolbox/widgets/_fileimport.py, adapted from
  Orange/data/io.py: the regular expression that reads the file name from the
  Content-Disposition header of a download.

The rest of the code, including the readers of every file format (also ARFF),
the statistical tests, the report, the sliding window validation, the Data
Table Pro widget (inspired by Orange's Data Table, without copying its code),
the widget icons and the documentation, is original work of the author. Other parts of
the add-on only import or subclass Orange classes and functions (such as
OWWidget, Validation, Results, results_merge or usable_scorers), which remain
part of Orange.
